_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**Inconsistent `refId` handling between `findSiblingComponent` and `findSiblingStory`.**

`findSiblingComponent` uses `refId` from state directly (line 353), while `findSiblingStory` uses `story.refId` from the resolved story data (line 374). This inconsistency could lead to different behavior when navigating between refs.

<details>
<summary>🔎 Suggested fix for consistency</summary>

```diff
  const findSiblingStory = (direction: Direction): StoryId | undefined => {
    const { filteredIndex, storyId, refs, refId } = store.getState();
    const story = api.getData(storyId, refId);

    if (!story) {
      return undefined;
    }

-   const hash = story.refId ? refs[story.refId].filteredIndex : filteredIndex;
+   const hash = refId ? refs[refId].filteredIndex || {} : filteredIndex;

    if (!hash) {
      return undefined;
    }

    return api.findSiblingStoryId(storyId, hash, direction, false);
  };
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In code/core/src/manager-api/modules/stories.ts around lines 345 to 380,
findSiblingComponent derives the index hash using refId from state while
findSiblingStory uses story.refId from the resolved story; make them consistent
by using story.refId in findSiblingComponent as well (i.e., after resolving
story, compute hash as story.refId ? refs[story.refId].filteredIndex :
filteredIndex) so both helpers target the same ref context when locating sibling
stories.
```

</details>

